[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was filed as one bug: the parser reads dates month first. Its
reports hold two bugs with two different fixes. Each one has its own ticket, and engineering
closed each one its own way.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 was not one issue. The parser fix did not touch the booking-v3 reports.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemSplit ticket={4471} {tickets} {oneDayMove} />

The table counts each report once, by id. The export repeats some reports, so a count of rows
is too high. Counts come from the desk's own cause logic (`causes.ts`), the same view as the
cause table on #4471.

## The two problems

**`parser`: the parser read month first.** Every tenant in #4471 writes the day first. The
shared parser read 07/04 as 4 July, so the day and the month swapped. This covers app, email
and booking-v2 form reports. Engineering fixed it: the parser now reads dd/mm for EU locales.

**`hint`: booking-v3 told people to type the month first.** The form printed `MM/DD/YYYY`
under its date field. People at day-first tenants followed it, and the form read their input
day first. The date flipped before the parser saw it, so the parser fix did not reach it.
Engineering will not fix the form: booking-v3 is retired.

**One-day moves.** A few `parser` reports describe a date that moved by one day, not a flip.
The desk read them that way (`desk-notes.json`) and still files them under `parser` by tenant.
If one-day moves come in after the parser fix, they are a time-zone bug: reopen the follow-up
ticket instead of merging them into a closed one.

## How the reports were placed

- **By tenant, not by intake tag.** Intake guesses the tag from the reporter's browser. The
  tenant's locale and booking form decide the cause (`causes.ts`). The tags disagree with the
  tenant in both groups, so the table shows them only for reference.
- **By what happened, not by subject.** Several subject lines appear under both problems.
  Matching on subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) cannot keep
  them apart.

## Lessons

- Before you merge a report into a big ticket, check how it came in and from which tenant,
  not only its subject line.
- Count by id, and group by tenant, not by the intake tag.

